alex: Quick Q — we're landing the convo streaming delta changes today. Are we renaming tool call payload field from `args` -> `params` in the delta messages, or keeping both? cc @rachel @noah

rachel: Plan is to accept both for now. Runtime will normalize incoming `args` or `params` -> internal `tool_params`. Deprecate `args` in the next major. Should be backcompat-safe for clients. :thumbsup:
\rachel: Example normalization (pseudo):
```json
{
  "delta": {
    "tool_call": {
      "name": "lookup_user",
      "params": { "user_id": 123 }
    }
  }
}
```

noah: Nice. For streaming partials — will we send partial `params` in successive delta events (i.e. incremental key additions), or only full objects when available?

rachel: We'll stream incremental key-level patches for large payloads to save latency. Rule: small payloads (<2KB) send full object; larger payloads stream as `params_delta` chunks with `seq` and `final` flags. Sample: 
```json
{
  "delta": {
    "tool_call": {
      "name": "generate_report",
      "params_delta": {"seq": 1, "chunk": "{\"filter\": \"status>200\"}" , "final": false }
    }
  }
}
```

jordan: SDK note: we'll need a helper that stitches `params_delta` chunks and validates final JSON. I'll put a small PR into sdk-js today and ping reviewers.

alex: Thanks. Also, any change to the streaming `delta.type` enum? Clients expect `tool_call`/`message`/`meta`.

rachel: No enum changes. We added `params_delta` as a field under `tool_call` only. No change to `delta.type` values.

noah: One more: telemetry — can we tag deltas with `params_mode: full|delta` so Optimize can surface cost impact?
\mrachel: Yep, we'll add `params_mode` on the envelope for both hosted and dedicated. Minimal perf hit.

alex: Timeline check — rachel, can we get rollout to staging by EOD so SDK tests can run?

rachel: Targeting staging canary in ~2h. I'll add migration notes to the PR and a short sample for compatibility.

sre-bot: deploy: canary deployed to staging (canary-3) — service: convo-stream — commit: f9c3e2d — monitor: https://infra/redwood/canary/3

alex: Perfect. Jordan/Noah if you see any flaky stitching in SDK tests ping me.

jordan: Will do, starting PR now.

noah: I'll add an e2e that simulates chunk reordering and duplicate seq numbers. Quick heads-up to reviewers.

alex: Great. Thanks all.
